<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Christ ist erstanden</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">12th century</span><span class="sg-chain-h">chorale derived from the sequence</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Christ lag in Todes Banden (Martin Luther)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">chorale derived from the sequence</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Metrical paraphrase (Jane E. Leeson)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">English paraphrase, sung to several hymn tunes</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Settings by Busnois, Josquin, Lassus, Willaert, Hans Buchner, Palestrina, Byrd, Perosi and Fernando de las Infantas</span><span class="sg-chain-h">musical settings</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Victimae paschali laudes (Jehan Revert)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting for four-part choir and organ</span></li></ul></section>
